From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: android-kitkat-tls12 <android-kitkat-tls12@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] OpenSSL 1.0.1u: openssl.config, openssl.version and the
 Android patches rebased

The recipe for the next commit (import_openssl.sh output); together they move
external/openssl from 1.0.1e (android-4.4.4_r2.0.1) to upstream 1.0.1u.

patches/: the 8 KitKat patches (progs, handshake_cutthrough, jsse, channelid,
eng_dyn_dirs, fix_clang_build, tls12_digests, alpn) ported by hand to the
reformatted 1.0.1u sources; each file starts with a note on what was adapted.
SSL_MODE_HANDSHAKE_CUTTHROUGH = 0x200 as in Android 5.1 (upstream
SSL_MODE_SEND_FALLBACK_SCSV = 0x80, SSL_MODE_SEND_CLIENTHELLO_TIME = 0x20).
early_ccs.patch dropped: CVE-2014-0224 is fixed upstream since 1.0.1h.

openssl.config: OPENSSL_PATCHES without early_ccs; progs without
crypto/ui/ui_openssl.c (1.0.1u defaults to TERMIOS on Linux); CONFIGURE_ARGS
+ enable-weak-ssl-ciphers (1.0.1s+ drops them by default; the 4.4 Java layer
lists those suites as supported and setEnabledCipherSuites() would throw);
UNNEEDED_SOURCES: entries that 1.0.1u no longer has (perl, the include links
of the disabled algorithms) removed, the new test sources added (as AOSP 5.1
did for constant_time_test.c, heartbeat_test.c, ssl_utst.c).

openssl.config arm: armcap.c and armv4cpuid.S built, OPENSSL_CPUID_OBJ
defined, mem_clr.c excluded, so the NEON paths of ghash-armv4 and
sha512-armv4 run (kktls_armcap_neon.patch: NEON from AT_HWCAP).
