+From: OpenSSL commit 9310d45087 by Matt Caswell (OpenSSL_1_0_2-stable, CVE-2018-0739), applied unchanged to OpenSSL 1.0.1u for android-kitkat-tls12
+Subject: cve-2018-0739
+
+Constructed ASN.1 types with a recursive definition (PKCS7) had no nesting
+limit, so a malicious BER blob could exhaust the stack in d2i (racoon IKE
+CERT payloads, PKCS#7 input of an app through NativeCrypto). Decoding now
+stops at depth 30 with ASN1_R_NESTED_TOO_DEEP. Fixed in 1.0.2o (2018-03),
+after the last 1.0.1 release.
